WEBVTT

00:00:33.780 --> 00:00:35.780
I really don't want to go.

00:00:35.780 --> 00:00:39.030
The King of Cavarin's invitation
to the Festival of the Spirit

00:00:39.030 --> 00:00:42.540
is just going to get us mixed up
in some kind of trouble.

00:00:42.540 --> 00:00:44.830
You're probably right.

00:00:44.830 --> 00:00:49.250
And that's assuming we even
make it to Cavarin in one piece.

00:00:49.250 --> 00:00:54.090
Right. Remnants of Marden's army
still lurk in the borderlands.

00:00:56.180 --> 00:00:58.350
Still, I really was shocked.

00:00:58.350 --> 00:01:00.510
Shocked? By what?

00:01:02.470 --> 00:01:04.310
Your hair.

00:01:05.770 --> 00:01:07.730
Truth be told, I was floored.

00:01:07.730 --> 00:01:10.020
It doesn't look like you dyed it.

00:01:10.020 --> 00:01:11.940
It's an old Flahm secret.

00:01:11.940 --> 00:01:15.990
What do you think, Wein?
Does white or black look better?

00:01:15.990 --> 00:01:18.570
Whoa! That's a trick question!

00:01:18.570 --> 00:01:21.830
Either answer will come back to haunt me!

00:01:21.830 --> 00:01:26.410
Actually, making light of
this will haunt you the most.

00:01:29.330 --> 00:01:30.210
White!

00:01:30.210 --> 00:01:32.340
That was unusually decisive.

00:01:32.340 --> 00:01:33.840
Come now, Ninym.

00:01:33.840 --> 00:01:38.090
I'm just an honest prince whose
creed is "always be decisive."

00:01:38.090 --> 00:01:39.180
Or so you say.

00:01:39.180 --> 00:01:42.220
So, white, huh?

00:01:42.220 --> 00:01:46.430
And here I thought
you'd love my hair like this.

00:01:46.430 --> 00:01:47.600
I'm so sad.

00:01:47.600 --> 00:01:51.400
Hey, no fair!
That's exactly what I was afraid of!

00:01:51.400 --> 00:01:53.110
There's nothing unfair about it.

00:01:53.110 --> 00:01:55.740
Any woman would feel this way.

00:01:55.740 --> 00:01:58.780
All right, now you've asked for it!

00:01:58.780 --> 00:02:00.070
Ninym!

00:02:00.070 --> 00:02:03.660
You did ask whether
I thought white or black looked better.

00:02:03.660 --> 00:02:06.410
But you didn't specify your hair!
In other words...

00:02:06.410 --> 00:02:07.540
In other words...?

00:02:07.540 --> 00:02:10.040
I meant your underwear color.

00:02:10.040 --> 00:02:11.210
Youch!

00:02:11.210 --> 00:02:14.750
Well, I guess that was partly my fault.

00:02:14.750 --> 00:02:16.510
Let's strike a bargain.

00:02:16.510 --> 00:02:20.050
After you were
the only one to land a strike?

00:02:20.050 --> 00:02:23.390
I'll make it up to you
by letting you stroke my hair.

00:02:23.390 --> 00:02:24.640
Huh?

00:02:24.640 --> 00:02:26.850
But not too hard.

00:02:26.850 --> 00:02:28.600
The color will come off.

00:02:28.600 --> 00:02:31.520
--Noogie time!
--Hey, stop it!

00:02:31.520 --> 00:02:33.110
Unbelievable.

00:02:33.110 --> 00:02:36.360
At least you didn't ruin it.

00:02:36.360 --> 00:02:41.240
Cavarin isn't the sort of place
where a Flahm should draw attention.

00:02:46.620 --> 00:02:49.120
I really <i>really </i>don't want to go.

00:02:52.960 --> 00:02:56.500
Let us halt today's
lesson there, shall we?

00:02:59.050 --> 00:03:00.590
Claudius.

00:03:00.590 --> 00:03:05.260
You're from the west, aren't you?
Do you know the Festival of the Spirit?

00:03:05.260 --> 00:03:06.890
But of course.

00:03:06.890 --> 00:03:10.560
Your Highness knows of the
Teachings of Levetia, I presume?

00:03:10.560 --> 00:03:12.940
It's a popular religion in the west.

00:03:12.940 --> 00:03:16.020
That is a perfectly fine summation.

00:03:16.020 --> 00:03:17.980
As for the Festival of the Spirit,

00:03:17.980 --> 00:03:21.820
it is a Levetian festival
held each spring.

00:03:21.820 --> 00:03:24.780
Levetia, the religion's founder
and blessed servant God,

00:03:24.780 --> 00:03:28.540
defeated a powerful demon
that had tormented humankind.

00:03:28.540 --> 00:03:32.120
The festival gives glory
and thanks for that great deed.

00:03:32.120 --> 00:03:34.830
Really?

00:03:34.830 --> 00:03:38.550
If Cavarin invited my brother
to a festival like that,

00:03:38.550 --> 00:03:42.050
maybe it means they want to
have better relations with Natra.

00:03:43.090 --> 00:03:44.470
Listen, Wein.

00:03:44.470 --> 00:03:46.010
I'll only say this once.

00:03:46.010 --> 00:03:50.230
When we get to Cavarin,
try your best to behave yourself.

00:03:50.230 --> 00:03:51.690
I know.

00:03:51.690 --> 00:03:56.270
Keep your cool even if caught off guard
by cultural and philosophical differences.

00:03:56.270 --> 00:03:58.980
Even I'm not <i>that </i>stupid.

00:03:58.980 --> 00:04:01.030
Then that's a promise?

00:04:01.030 --> 00:04:02.240
Sure!

00:04:02.240 --> 00:04:05.410
And have you ever known me
to break a promise?

00:04:05.410 --> 00:04:07.830
All the time.

00:04:07.830 --> 00:04:10.120
Well then, root for me to change!

00:04:11.450 --> 00:04:15.790
Break <i>this </i>promise, and I'll cram
potatoes in every orifice of your body.

00:04:15.790 --> 00:04:20.670
Personally, I don't think you
should be wasting food like that.

00:04:20.670 --> 00:04:23.880
Your Highness,
forgive me for interrupting.

00:04:23.880 --> 00:04:28.970
We will soon be arriving
at the Jilaat Gold Mine.

00:04:28.970 --> 00:04:30.680
Finally!

00:04:35.400 --> 00:04:38.940
It seems all the facilities
and tunnels damaged in the war

00:04:38.940 --> 00:04:40.650
have been nearly restored.

00:04:40.650 --> 00:04:45.110
Yes, Highness. We're mining even more
gold thanks to our additional labor.

00:04:45.110 --> 00:04:50.580
Along with our gold mining,
we're starting to seek out new veins.

00:04:50.580 --> 00:04:52.540
New veins!

00:04:52.540 --> 00:04:55.750
Just hearing that makes
my heart dance for joy!

00:04:55.750 --> 00:04:57.830
Wein, your face.

00:04:59.710 --> 00:05:03.260
Don't rush the mining work at
the expense of proper management.

00:05:03.260 --> 00:05:07.430
High worker turnover attracts
more unsavory characters.

00:05:07.430 --> 00:05:10.180
Yes, I will keep that in mind.

00:05:12.390 --> 00:05:17.350
We didn't have to worry about
such things as long as Hagal was well.

00:05:17.350 --> 00:05:19.900
His retirement was most unexpected.

00:05:19.900 --> 00:05:24.820
He was like a god of battle
in the recent war.

00:05:24.820 --> 00:05:28.910
He himself said you can't
fight off old age forever.

00:05:28.910 --> 00:05:30.530
I won't try to stop him.

00:05:30.530 --> 00:05:33.830
What is General Hagal doing now?

00:05:33.830 --> 00:05:38.000
I bet he's enjoying the retired life,
stuff like farming and whatnot.

00:05:38.000 --> 00:05:40.210
Farming?

00:05:40.210 --> 00:05:42.750
Truth be told, I wanted to stop him.

00:05:42.750 --> 00:05:47.130
In the general's absence, the
nobility is showing signs of rebellion.

00:05:47.130 --> 00:05:49.260
Or so the reports say.

00:05:53.010 --> 00:05:55.060
Ibis, was it?

00:05:55.060 --> 00:05:59.100
Is it true Prince Wein has been
invited to the Festival of the Spirit?

00:05:59.100 --> 00:06:01.230
There can be no mistake.

00:06:01.230 --> 00:06:05.320
Information is the life's blood
of those who sell it for a living.

00:06:05.320 --> 00:06:09.570
With Hagal gone and the prince abroad,
it's our chance to raise an army!

00:06:09.570 --> 00:06:11.870
We needn't heed the royal family now!

00:06:11.870 --> 00:06:15.330
We shall form the new power base of Natra!

00:06:15.330 --> 00:06:19.540
Muster the troops! We shall deal
a heavy blow against the royal house!

00:06:19.540 --> 00:06:21.540
Now is the time to rise up!

00:06:21.540 --> 00:06:24.960
May you fare well upon your path...

00:06:24.960 --> 00:06:26.550
Prince Wein.

00:06:32.510 --> 00:06:35.560
The enemy's upon us! To arms!

00:06:38.350 --> 00:06:40.940
Godspeed, Your Highness!

00:06:44.650 --> 00:06:47.190
Soldiers disguised as brigands.

00:06:47.190 --> 00:06:52.450
They're most likely from Cavarin
or remnants of Marden's forces.

00:06:52.450 --> 00:06:54.780
But it's impossible
to say which right now.

00:06:54.780 --> 00:06:57.120
We'll just have to roll the dice!

00:06:57.120 --> 00:07:00.460
Wein! The area ahead is
controlled by Mardenian remnants!

00:07:00.460 --> 00:07:02.580
Full speed ahead!

00:07:02.580 --> 00:07:06.170
--You sure?!
--Yes. If I'm reading this right...

00:07:14.970 --> 00:07:17.020
Wein! I'll buy us some time.

00:07:17.020 --> 00:07:19.560
No need for that. Look.

00:07:26.780 --> 00:07:29.110
Retreat. Retreat!

00:07:30.570 --> 00:07:32.530
Mardenian remnants.

00:07:32.530 --> 00:07:35.410
So it would seem.

00:07:35.410 --> 00:07:39.870
I am the crown prince of Natra,
Wein Salema Arbalest.

00:07:40.790 --> 00:07:46.250
I've come to meet with Prince Helmut,
commander of the Free Mardenian Forces.

00:07:46.250 --> 00:07:48.550
I wish to speak with him!

00:08:05.020 --> 00:08:07.770
You are the crown prince of Natran?

00:08:09.650 --> 00:08:14.820
I am Zeno, and I speak for
His Highness, Prince Helmut.

00:08:14.820 --> 00:08:18.950
The prince cannot receive you.
He is unwell and bedridden.

00:08:18.950 --> 00:08:21.370
Prince Helmut is unwell?

00:08:21.370 --> 00:08:25.710
Cavarin seized him when our capital fell,

00:08:25.710 --> 00:08:28.960
and the fiends put a torch to his face.

00:08:31.590 --> 00:08:36.180
Now, tell me, Prince Wein.
Why have you come to our land?

00:08:36.180 --> 00:08:38.810
I would have the truth from you.

00:08:38.810 --> 00:08:40.640
I'm on my way to Cavarin's capital

00:08:40.640 --> 00:08:43.810
to take part in the
Festival of the Spirit.

00:08:45.020 --> 00:08:48.110
You do understand the meaning
of what you just said?

00:08:48.110 --> 00:08:51.690
Would you care to rethink
your words, Prince Wein?

00:08:51.690 --> 00:08:54.150
I was merely stating a fact.

00:08:54.150 --> 00:08:56.160
What do I need to rethink?

00:08:56.160 --> 00:08:58.120
In that case...

00:08:59.530 --> 00:09:03.370
...I have no choice but to cut
you down where you stand!

00:09:09.790 --> 00:09:12.800
Prince Wein, I have a question for you.

00:09:12.800 --> 00:09:15.300
Sure, ask away.

00:09:15.300 --> 00:09:20.600
He not only escaped enemy territory alive,
he also forged a temporary alliance.

00:09:20.600 --> 00:09:24.020
I must once again take my
hat off to His Highness's audacity.

00:09:24.020 --> 00:09:28.190
I really thought it
was all over this time.

00:09:30.980 --> 00:09:32.860
You find something amusing?

00:09:32.860 --> 00:09:35.900
Oh, no, I meant no disrespect.

00:09:35.900 --> 00:09:38.950
Please allow me one question.

00:09:38.950 --> 00:09:41.620
What will happen if you kill me?

00:09:41.620 --> 00:09:44.040
It will prevent a
Cavarinian-Natran alliance.

00:09:44.040 --> 00:09:45.370
And then?

00:09:45.370 --> 00:09:51.250
Do you truly believe your freedom
forces can defeat Cavarin?

00:09:51.250 --> 00:09:54.300
They can muster an
army over 20,000 strong.

00:09:54.300 --> 00:09:57.220
What is your forces' present strength?

00:09:57.220 --> 00:10:02.310
I'd guess only about two to
three thousand if I'm being generous.

00:10:02.310 --> 00:10:04.430
Once winter comes to an end,

00:10:04.430 --> 00:10:08.100
the full force of Cavarin
will bear down on you.

00:10:08.100 --> 00:10:11.560
Do the Free Mardenian Forces
have a plan to counter that?

00:10:14.900 --> 00:10:17.900
So let me get this straight.

00:10:17.900 --> 00:10:22.120
You're saying we might as well free you
because we're already goners?

00:10:22.120 --> 00:10:23.490
Not at all.

00:10:23.490 --> 00:10:27.830
I have a proposal far more
beneficial to all concerned.

00:10:27.830 --> 00:10:29.250
A proposal?

00:10:29.250 --> 00:10:30.460
Indeed.

00:10:30.460 --> 00:10:36.630
Lady Zeno, do you have anyone
you could send with us to Cavarin?

00:10:36.630 --> 00:10:38.720
I don't follow.

00:10:38.720 --> 00:10:41.680
The brigands that attacked us

00:10:41.680 --> 00:10:45.640
were most likely Cavarinian troops.

00:10:45.640 --> 00:10:47.140
I don't understand.

00:10:47.140 --> 00:10:49.980
Why would Cavarin do such a thing?

00:10:49.980 --> 00:10:54.480
That is as yet unknown,
which is why I'm offering a proposal.

00:10:54.480 --> 00:10:57.610
I will not halt my journey to Cavarin.

00:10:57.610 --> 00:10:59.950
But whatever awaits me there,

00:10:59.950 --> 00:11:04.830
it may be in my best interest to ally
with your Free Mardenian Forces.

00:11:04.830 --> 00:11:09.910
If so, having someone from your forces
will send a message loud and clear.

00:11:09.910 --> 00:11:13.460
The Holy Elites, influential
figures from across the land,

00:11:13.460 --> 00:11:15.920
are gathering in the capital of Cavarin.

00:11:15.920 --> 00:11:18.050
Security is no doubt tight.

00:11:18.050 --> 00:11:22.760
But a member of a diplomatic delegation
should have no problem entering.

00:11:22.760 --> 00:11:27.520
If we can make contact with them,
we might be able to get their help.

00:11:30.440 --> 00:11:34.110
I must admit your proposal
is worth some thought.

00:11:34.110 --> 00:11:38.530
--So then--
--However, I cannot help
but remain uneasy.

00:11:38.530 --> 00:11:43.490
I don't know if this is all
an act to escape our grasp.

00:11:43.490 --> 00:11:46.240
I don't even know if I can trust you.

00:11:46.240 --> 00:11:48.290
That's what you're worried about?

00:11:48.290 --> 00:11:50.210
Tell me, how is that a problem?

00:11:50.210 --> 00:11:51.250
Come again?

00:11:51.250 --> 00:11:52.750
Listen, Lady Zeno.

00:11:52.750 --> 00:11:57.710
Trust gains value when there
is the potential for treachery.

00:11:57.710 --> 00:12:01.260
Maybe you're being fed lies.
Maybe you're being tricked.

00:12:01.260 --> 00:12:04.550
But stifling those fears
and choosing to trust

00:12:04.550 --> 00:12:07.470
is how you touch another's heart!

00:12:09.270 --> 00:12:11.060
I'll ask you once more.

00:12:11.060 --> 00:12:15.610
Are you truly unable to trust me?

00:12:15.610 --> 00:12:17.110
Very well.

00:12:17.110 --> 00:12:22.030
I will inform Prince Helmut that
you are a man worthy of our trust.

00:12:22.030 --> 00:12:28.620
I have no doubt that he will come
to the same conclusion before long.

00:12:31.040 --> 00:12:33.540
Ninym! Come have a look!

00:12:39.800 --> 00:12:41.210
Is that...?

00:12:41.210 --> 00:12:44.880
Tristoria, the royal capital of Cavarin.

00:12:45.890 --> 00:12:49.140
I've never seen it before.
It sure is beautiful.

00:12:54.600 --> 00:12:56.940
Now, about tomorrow.

00:12:56.940 --> 00:13:01.150
I'll be meeting with
King Ordalasse of Cavarin.

00:13:01.150 --> 00:13:04.320
As my personal guard,
I'll take Raklum and a few others.

00:13:04.320 --> 00:13:05.610
I'll leave you to choose.

00:13:05.610 --> 00:13:06.820
Highness.

00:13:06.820 --> 00:13:09.490
Ninym will head the team
that gathers information.

00:13:09.490 --> 00:13:11.750
Choose whomever you see fit.

00:13:11.750 --> 00:13:12.950
Yes, Your Highness.

00:13:12.950 --> 00:13:17.500
Lady Zeno, what will you do?

00:13:17.500 --> 00:13:18.840
Zeno?

00:13:18.840 --> 00:13:20.050
Forgive me.

00:13:20.050 --> 00:13:24.510
I thought I'd go gather information
with my people tomorrow.

00:13:24.510 --> 00:13:25.840
I see.

00:13:25.840 --> 00:13:28.930
You should work with Ninym if need be.

00:13:51.410 --> 00:13:55.080
Good sir, are you
the special envoy from Natra?

00:13:55.080 --> 00:13:58.290
This must all be so
new to provincials like you.

00:13:58.290 --> 00:14:02.670
I hope you enjoy the sights.

00:14:02.670 --> 00:14:04.550
Who might that be?

00:14:04.550 --> 00:14:09.090
Levert has long served as
a general in our kingdom's army.

00:14:09.090 --> 00:14:11.850
A general, eh?

00:14:11.850 --> 00:14:13.930
Raklum, calm yourself.

00:14:13.930 --> 00:14:17.140
It's just a local custom.

00:14:17.140 --> 00:14:17.980
Highness.

00:14:17.980 --> 00:14:22.610
Take a careful look
at that man who is with him.

00:14:22.610 --> 00:14:25.400
When we were ambushed on the way here,

00:14:25.400 --> 00:14:29.240
the apparent leader took
an arrow to his right arm.

00:14:29.240 --> 00:14:31.240
Same arm. Same face.

00:14:31.240 --> 00:14:33.120
You're not suggesting...

00:14:33.120 --> 00:14:35.160
I can't be sure yet,

00:14:35.160 --> 00:14:38.120
but we must consider
the possibility for now.

00:14:38.120 --> 00:14:39.540
Highness!

00:14:43.290 --> 00:14:46.630
So good of you to travel all this way.

00:14:46.630 --> 00:14:51.260
I bid you my warmest
of welcomes, Prince Wein.

00:14:51.260 --> 00:14:54.760
I am King Ordalasse of Cavarin.

00:14:54.760 --> 00:14:56.310
Y-Yes, Your Majesty.

00:14:56.310 --> 00:15:00.190
I've always wished we could
meet to exchange words.

00:15:00.190 --> 00:15:03.150
I'm thankful my wish came true.

00:15:03.150 --> 00:15:05.690
But this is no place
for a fine conversation.

00:15:05.690 --> 00:15:08.280
Let us seek a more suitable location.

00:15:08.280 --> 00:15:11.780
And there are some others
I'd like you to meet.

00:15:12.870 --> 00:15:14.700
What now, Your Highness?

00:15:14.700 --> 00:15:17.250
It's too late to say no.

00:15:27.800 --> 00:15:29.840
Don't move.

00:15:29.840 --> 00:15:33.140
--Let me go.
--You know I can't do that.

00:15:36.060 --> 00:15:37.140
Where are we?

00:15:37.140 --> 00:15:40.890
It's one of the hideouts
our spies use while they're here.

00:15:40.890 --> 00:15:43.810
Is inviting me here a good idea?

00:15:43.810 --> 00:15:45.900
Probably not.

00:15:45.900 --> 00:15:49.570
But I needed somewhere safe
to talk some sense into you.

00:15:49.570 --> 00:15:52.280
That man you were about to assassinate,

00:15:52.280 --> 00:15:55.740
he once served Marden.

00:15:55.740 --> 00:15:57.620
Holonyeh.

00:15:57.620 --> 00:16:03.330
Did he gain the good graces of Cavarin
in return for betraying Marden, or...?

00:16:03.330 --> 00:16:07.130
If he...! If that man
had not betrayed us...!

00:16:07.130 --> 00:16:10.090
If not for that traitor,
my father would still...!

00:16:10.090 --> 00:16:13.050
You lost your family in the attack?

00:16:13.050 --> 00:16:17.180
Th-That's right.
They were caught up in the fighting.

00:16:17.180 --> 00:16:23.810
I understand why you feel that way,
but I can't allow you to assassinate him.

00:16:23.810 --> 00:16:24.850
Fine.

00:16:24.850 --> 00:16:28.820
I've other matters to look into,
so I'll put off killing him for now.

00:16:28.820 --> 00:16:31.190
That would be most helpful.

00:16:31.190 --> 00:16:33.660
Still, betraying one's own land is...

00:16:33.660 --> 00:16:35.200
Is what?

00:16:35.200 --> 00:16:39.870
Never mind. I was just thinking of
what Wein will say when he finds out.

00:16:40.950 --> 00:16:44.420
Allow me to introduce Prince Wein!

00:16:44.420 --> 00:16:47.420
Whoa, whoa! Aren't they the...

00:16:47.420 --> 00:16:50.760
They are the pillars
of the Levetian religion.

00:16:50.760 --> 00:16:56.850
All of the Holy Elites are here in Cavarin
for the Gathering of the Chosen.

00:16:56.850 --> 00:17:00.810
Wait a second! Why the hell
was I even invited here?!

00:17:00.810 --> 00:17:04.850
What is the meaning
of this, King Ordalasse?

00:17:04.850 --> 00:17:07.150
Why is the Natran prince here?

00:17:07.150 --> 00:17:10.480
So they're just as shocked as I am!

00:17:10.480 --> 00:17:13.490
This is bad, really bad!

00:17:13.490 --> 00:17:15.610
I have zero control of the situation.

00:17:15.610 --> 00:17:20.790
I have a proposal for you,
the Holy Elites.

00:17:20.790 --> 00:17:26.790
I nominate Wein Salema Arbalest
to join you as your newest member.

00:17:26.790 --> 00:17:30.670
I nominate...

00:17:32.090 --> 00:17:37.220
What the actual hell?!

00:17:38.300 --> 00:17:40.930
I can't take it anymore! This is insane!

00:17:40.930 --> 00:17:42.520
Why's this happening?!

00:17:42.520 --> 00:17:44.850
Give me a break already!

00:17:44.850 --> 00:17:46.850
What happened?

00:17:46.850 --> 00:17:51.020
King Ordalasse nominated me
to join the Holy Elites.

00:17:51.020 --> 00:17:53.650
Huh? You're joking, right?

00:17:53.650 --> 00:17:56.530
Nope. I'm serious. Dead serious.

00:17:56.530 --> 00:17:58.320
To join the Holy Elites,

00:17:58.320 --> 00:18:01.950
one must be of the bloodline
of the religion's founder, Levetia,

00:18:01.950 --> 00:18:03.830
or a chief disciple thereof.

00:18:03.830 --> 00:18:05.790
Unfortunately, I check that box.

00:18:05.790 --> 00:18:09.380
The Natran royal family can
trace its lineage back to Caleus,

00:18:09.380 --> 00:18:11.420
a chief disciple of Levetia.

00:18:11.420 --> 00:18:13.300
So, what now?

00:18:13.300 --> 00:18:15.510
Will you really become a Holy Elite?

00:18:15.510 --> 00:18:18.090
I do see value in that.

00:18:18.090 --> 00:18:19.390
That's true.

00:18:19.390 --> 00:18:24.810
The current members of the Holy Elites
are all bigwigs from the western lands.

00:18:24.810 --> 00:18:27.480
It wouldn't hurt to make some connections.

00:18:27.480 --> 00:18:31.820
I'll start with some legwork and make
courtesy calls to each of them.

00:18:31.820 --> 00:18:33.480
Wein.

00:18:33.480 --> 00:18:37.950
Would you take Zeno
along on those courtesy calls?

00:18:39.820 --> 00:18:43.240
This is our chance to make contact
with Holy Elites from many lands.

00:18:43.240 --> 00:18:46.120
Slay them or let them live.
It's your choice, Zeno.

00:18:46.120 --> 00:18:47.660
Understood.

00:18:47.660 --> 00:18:52.380
I'll plead our case in the hopes
that we'll get help from some quarter.

00:18:54.420 --> 00:18:57.720
First stop, the famed Caldmellia.

00:18:59.300 --> 00:19:03.560
Male chauvinism is rife in the
western lands of the continent.

00:19:03.560 --> 00:19:07.180
And due to literal interpretations
of the Teachings of Levetia,

00:19:07.180 --> 00:19:09.850
women aren't accepted in high places.

00:19:09.850 --> 00:19:13.230
But you, Caldmellia,
somehow rose through the ranks.

00:19:13.230 --> 00:19:15.940
You've risen as high
as one may without descending

00:19:15.940 --> 00:19:18.070
from Levetia or a chief disciple.

00:19:18.070 --> 00:19:20.570
You're now Director
of the Bureau of Teachings.

00:19:26.200 --> 00:19:29.790
Your Highness,
I truly understand how you feel.

00:19:29.790 --> 00:19:32.880
With the full authority vested
in me by His Holiness,

00:19:32.880 --> 00:19:36.960
I recognize you as a suitable
candidate for the Holy Elites.

00:19:36.960 --> 00:19:41.050
--So then--
--However, I do have one condition.

00:19:41.050 --> 00:19:42.970
What would you have of me?

00:19:42.970 --> 00:19:47.310
According to King Ordalasse,
you went to war with Marden

00:19:47.310 --> 00:19:51.690
to free its people
from the tyranny of their king.

00:19:51.690 --> 00:19:56.150
That good deed makes you worthy
of joining the Holy Elites.

00:19:56.150 --> 00:19:58.650
Of course, that's not true.

00:19:58.650 --> 00:20:00.280
It's just a justification.

00:20:00.280 --> 00:20:05.740
But I cannot support your nomination
unless you complete their salvation.

00:20:05.740 --> 00:20:09.790
What? Complete their salvation?

00:20:09.790 --> 00:20:13.080
But Natra took Marden's
royal capital along with Cavarin.

00:20:13.080 --> 00:20:17.090
Yet remnants of their army
still live, do they not?

00:20:18.050 --> 00:20:22.010
The persecution of the
Levetian faithful persists in Marden.

00:20:22.010 --> 00:20:26.810
And it is those remnants
who continue to defy us.

00:20:27.560 --> 00:20:32.980
They must all be slain to restore peace
to the hearts of the faithful.

00:20:32.980 --> 00:20:35.480
We must then publicly
display their corpses

00:20:35.480 --> 00:20:37.650
and throw them into
the flames of damnation.

00:20:37.650 --> 00:20:40.150
Wouldn't you agree?

00:20:40.150 --> 00:20:44.360
You there. Is something the matter?

00:20:44.360 --> 00:20:49.830
You may be seated should
you find yourself feeling unwell.

00:20:49.830 --> 00:20:54.750
P-Please don't mind me.
There is no cause for concern.

00:20:54.750 --> 00:20:59.050
I see. So that's how it's going to be.

00:21:01.210 --> 00:21:04.180
It seems I really struck a nerve.

00:21:05.550 --> 00:21:10.100
Was that sufficient payback
for the arm he claimed, Owl?

00:21:10.100 --> 00:21:13.100
You enjoy this far too much,
Lady Caldmellia.

00:21:13.100 --> 00:21:18.940
I feared the worst should
his attendant resort to violence.

00:21:18.940 --> 00:21:23.450
Wouldn't it have been
splendid if that had happened?

00:21:25.200 --> 00:21:29.330
Ninym, I want you to look into
Levert and his inner circle tomorrow.

00:21:29.330 --> 00:21:33.200
Was he behind the attack on our way here?

00:21:33.200 --> 00:21:36.790
Or it might have been his faction.

00:21:36.790 --> 00:21:39.750
Holonyeh.

00:21:39.750 --> 00:21:41.670
"As instructed..."

00:21:41.670 --> 00:21:45.050
"...the mansion's floorplans."

00:21:45.050 --> 00:21:47.260
"It's really happening."

00:21:47.260 --> 00:21:49.220
"The king's bloodline..."

00:21:49.220 --> 00:21:52.890
"Your... traitor will be..."?

00:21:52.890 --> 00:21:55.480
"With the prince out of the way..."

00:21:56.730 --> 00:21:59.520
"...we can defeat Natra"?!

00:22:04.860 --> 00:22:06.650
Filthy devils!

00:22:11.330 --> 00:22:15.580
Are you serious about elevating
the prince to the Holy Elites?

00:22:15.580 --> 00:22:20.250
Yes. I'll be most delighted if he
eliminates those Marden remnants.

00:22:20.250 --> 00:22:24.340
With all due respect,
the prince is truly a threat.

00:22:24.340 --> 00:22:27.180
Should he gain a position
of power in the west,

00:22:27.180 --> 00:22:30.140
he will surely be your bane,
Lady Caldmellia.

00:22:30.140 --> 00:22:32.720
Is that not a good thing?

00:22:35.140 --> 00:22:39.350
May you find that it's all too late.
